%define _unpackaged_files_terminate_build 1

Name: yarn
Version: 1.22.22
Release: alt2
Summary: Fast, reliable, and secure dependency management
Group: Development/Tools
License: BSD-2-Clause
Url: https://yarnpkg.com

# Source0 is regenerated from the upstream sources with vendored node_modules
# (devDependencies reduced, js-yaml bumped to 4.x and mkdirp pinned via the
# prebundle patches, dependencies refreshed via `yarn install` + `yarn audit fix`)
# so that security fixes in the bundled dependencies take effect. The vendored
# node_modules is the BUILD toolchain only: %%build webpacks src/ + the patched
# node_modules into a single self-contained lib/cli.js, and only that bundle is
# shipped (no node_modules at runtime). Generated by yarn-tarball.sh.
Source: yarn-v%version.tar.gz
Source1: yarn-tarball.sh
# Prebundle patches: applied by yarn-tarball.sh while regenerating Source0
# (not applied during the package build). Shipped for reproducibility.
Source2: 0001-yarn-no-eslint.prebundle.patch
Source3: 0002-yarn-no-commitizen.prebundle.patch
Source4: 0003-yarn-no-jest.prebundle.patch
Source5: 0004-yarn-js-yaml.prebundle.patch
Source6: 0005-yarn-mkdirp-resolution.prebundle.patch

# Security fixes in bundled runtime dependencies, webpacked into lib/cli.js
Patch0: CVE-2023-26136.patch
Patch1: CVE-2025-8263.patch
# Security fixes in yarn itself (src/), webpacked into lib/cli.js
Patch2: CVE-2025-8262.patch
Patch3: CVE-2025-9308.patch
# Adapt yarn to the js-yaml 4.x API (paired with the js-yaml prebundle bump)
Patch4: yarn-jsyaml4.patch

BuildRequires(pre): rpm-macros-nodejs
BuildRequires: node npm
%filter_from_requires /^.usr.bin.node/d
Requires: node

BuildArch: noarch

%description
Fast, reliable, and secure dependency management.
Yarn: Fast, reliable, and secure dependency management.

%prep
%setup -n %name-%version
%patch0 -p1
%patch1 -p1
%patch2 -p1
%patch3 -p1
%patch4 -p1

%build
# Webpack src/ + the patched node_modules into a single self-contained bundle
# (artifacts/yarn-legacy-%version.js). The vendored node_modules provides the
# build toolchain, so no network access is required.
npm run build-bundle

%install
mkdir -p %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/lib %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/bin %buildroot%_bindir

# Ship only the self-contained bundle (mirrors upstream scripts/build-dist.sh).
install -p -m644 artifacts/yarn-legacy-%version.js %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/lib/cli.js
install -p -m644 node_modules/v8-compile-cache/v8-compile-cache.js %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/lib/v8-compile-cache.js
install -p -m755 bin/yarn.js %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/bin/yarn.js
install -p -m644 README.md LICENSE %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/

# A trimmed package.json (metadata only, no build dependency lists).
node -e 'const p=require("./package.json"); for (const k of ["dependencies","devDependencies","resolutions","jest","scripts"]) delete p[k]; require("fs").writeFileSync(process.argv[1], JSON.stringify(p,null,2)+"\n")' \
    %buildroot%nodejs_sitelib/%name/package.json

ln -s %nodejs_sitelib/%name/bin/yarn.js %buildroot%_bindir/%name
ln -s %nodejs_sitelib/%name/bin/yarn.js %buildroot%_bindir/yarnpkg

%files
%doc README.md
%_bindir/*
%nodejs_sitelib/%name

%changelog
* Thu Jun 26 2026 Alexey Shabalin <shaba@altlinux.org> 1.22.22-alt2
- Rebuild the self-contained lib/cli.js bundle from source against a refreshed,
  security-patched dependency tree instead of shipping the upstream prebuilt
  bundle (devDependencies reduced, js-yaml bumped to 4.x and mkdirp pinned via
  prebundle patches, dependencies refreshed via `yarn install`+`yarn audit fix`).
- The refreshed dependency tree also pulls newer, fixed versions of other
  bundled runtime modules; build-only dependencies are no longer shipped.
- Fixes:
  + CVE-2025-8262 ReDoS in explodeHostedGitFragment (yarn hosted-git-resolver)
  + CVE-2025-9308 ReDoS in RequestManager.setOptions cafile parsing (yarn)
  + CVE-2025-8263 predictable multipart boundary in bundled form-data
  + CVE-2023-26136 prototype pollution in bundled tough-cookie

